DESCRIPTION
===========

|YKOEquipment loadouts are named presets for your worn armour and wielded
weapons. Save your current equipment with |CKBloadout save <name>|YKO, then
use |CKBloadout use <name>|YKO to return to that setup.

A loadout is a complete equipment state. Standard armour or weapons not named
in the preset are removed when it is used, which allows a preset to preserve
intentionally empty slots. Installed cyberware and other internal equipment
are never changed.

Every saved item must be directly in your inventory before a loadout can be
used. Loadouts do not retrieve items from containers, banks, rooms, or other
storage, and they never clone or replace missing gear. If an item is missing
or cannot be identified safely, nothing is changed.

Normal equipment rules remain in force. Cursed items, scripted restrictions,
guild requirements, race and size limits, shields, and weapon combinations can
prevent a switch. If a restriction stops a switch after it begins, DarkWind
attempts to restore your original equipment and tells you whether that
restoration succeeded.

You cannot switch loadouts during combat, while dead, or while phased out.
You may save up to ten loadouts. Names may contain up to twenty lowercase
letters, numbers, underscores, or hyphens.

The |CKBgearset|YKO command is an alias for |CKBloadout|YKO.

